 value-based drift term and an additive noise is investigated: 

\begin{equation}
\begin{cases}
dY_t = \big(B_1(Y_t)\pm B_2(Y_t)\big)dt + \big(B_3(Y_t)\pm B_4(Y_t)\big)dB_t \\
Y_0 = y_0
\end{equation}

where $B_i$ are bounded, Lipschitz continuous functions and $B_1, B_3$ are odd functions.

The existence and uniqueness of the solution is proven, and the behavior of the solution as $y_0$ tends to infinity or negative infinity is analyzed.
